# Everything below is pending the UI rewrite slice (issues/rewrite_architecture.md
# Sections 3-4). Left in the working tree but out of the load list until each file's replacement
# lands, since they depend on the old Preydator.lua monolith that bootstrap now replaces.
# UI\EditMode.lua                       (was Modules\EditMode.lua) -- permanently not needed,
#   confirmed by the product owner (Decisions Log items 38/39): the entire desired behavior
#   (drag the bar during Blizzard Edit Mode, return to whatever the lock checkbox says on
#   exit) is already built into UI\BarFrame.lua (frame:EnableMouse((not lockBar) or
#   editModeActive)); no floating quick-settings window wanted at all.
# UI\ReportWindow.lua                   (was Modules\ReportWindow.lua) -- superseded by the
#   working /pd chat+BugSack diagnostic flow (Core\SlashCommands.lua); not being built
#   (Decisions Log item 38).
# Modules\Settings.lua (old, ~3600-line monolith) is not superseded by UI\SettingsPanel.lua's
#   General/Bar Display/Bar Colors/Text & Labels/Sound & Alerts/Hunt Scanner/Advanced
#   categories -- it's still cited as a live design/port reference in
#   issues/bar_rendering_research.md, so it's not orphaned/forgotten, just not on the load
#   list. Don't git rm it while that reference doc still points at it.
# Modules\HuntScanner.lua (old, 5045-line monolith) is only PARTIALLY superseded -- the
#   MVP scan/list/select/zone-derivation core AND the new HuntTablePanel.lua (icon/name/
#   zone/Accept rows only) now live above, but grouping/sorting and achievement-signal
#   matching (full-scope per Section 15) are still only in the old file -- reward display
#   is now fully covered by the new files above (Decisions Log item 19). Don't git rm it yet.
# Core\SlashCommands.lua (/pd inspect|qinspect|hinspect|pinspect [bs]) replaces the old
#   Modules\DebugInspect.lua/Modules\SlashCommands.lua slash-command glue -- report content
#   lives in Core\Runtime\DiagnosticsRuntime.lua, scoped to State/Settings/Adapters/
#   HuntScanner data only, no bar-frame/label-frame geometry (Decisions Log item 20).
